    "confidence": "high",
    "summary": "Paterson's corner infrastructure was unlike any prior split: many corners carry TWO tactile surface indicators almost side by side, offset roughly 60-90 degrees, one per crossing direction. The reviewer's impression is that the model under-identified these paired corners, typically firing once where the GT now records two ramps; the reviewer zoomed in per corner and credited a true positive where a detection legitimately covered one of the pair. Second impression: many distant ramps were missed. Reviewer-rated confidence is HIGH: the rubric fit, the judgment calls were minor, and a second rater would be expected to land within the reported confidence intervals.",
    "caveats": [
      "Paired tactile surface indicators. Where a corner carried two TSIs (one per crossing direction, offset ~60-90 degrees), each was marked as its own ramp. The model usually fired once per such corner, so the partner surface lands as a missed mark. This is a recall effect, not a precision one - it produced only 1 duplicate verdict (vs budapest's 7) - and is believed to be a meaningful contributor to the 161 missed/unsure-missed marks, alongside distance.",
      "Distant ramps. Reviewer impression of substantial far-field misses, echoing the annapolis far-field finding. Impression, not measurement - the Phase-4 distance analysis should quantify it."
    ]
  },
